        <item>
            <title>0.15.83</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:52:58 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>244</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.83</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>A meeting that happened to be titled &quot;Daily standup&quot;, &quot;All hands, Q1 review&quot; or one of a few other old sample names could disappear after a restart. Real meetings are never removed that way any more.</li>
<li>A recording where Corder heard no speech is moved to Archive as before, but its audio now stays there for the full 7 days instead of being deleted right away, so you can still listen to it or transcribe it again.</li>
<li>Recording no longer stops when the screen goes dark. An in-person meeting on a laptop nobody touches keeps recording, and the Mac does not doze off mid-meeting.</li>
<li>If screen sharing ends while you record with video (the &quot;Stop Sharing&quot; button, or the screen permission changes), the video stops there but the audio keeps recording and you can stop it as usual. Before, the recording got stuck and could not be stopped.</li>
<li>Old original audio tracks are only cleaned up when the playback copy is complete.</li>
<li>Renaming a meeting while it records or transcribes no longer moves its folder in the middle of the work; the folder follows the new name when it is done.</li>
<li>Starting a recording right when Corder noticed a call no longer fails with &quot;Already recording&quot;.</li>
<li>Fixed a rare crash with on-device transcription while the model was still being prepared for the first time.</li>
<li>If your audio device changes right as a recording starts (for example Bluetooth headphones switching on), your microphone keeps recording.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
